;; improvy.app — BIND zone file, for Cloudflare's "Import DNS records".
;;
;; What it sets up: the apex (improvy.app) points at GitHub Pages' four
;; anycast addresses, in both IPv4 and IPv6, and www is a CNAME to the Pages
;; host, which serves the repository named by public/CNAME.
;;
;; TTL 1 means "Auto" in Cloudflare.
;;
;; IMPORTANT, on import: leave "Proxy imported DNS records" UNCHECKED. With
;; Cloudflare's proxy on, GitHub cannot complete the HTTP challenge and never
;; issues the certificate — and improvy.app is a .app domain, which browsers
;; refuse to open without HTTPS. Turn the proxy on later, once the padlock
;; works, if you want it at all.

;; A records — GitHub Pages, IPv4
improvy.app.	1	IN	A	185.199.108.153
improvy.app.	1	IN	A	185.199.109.153
improvy.app.	1	IN	A	185.199.110.153
improvy.app.	1	IN	A	185.199.111.153

;; AAAA records — the same, IPv6
improvy.app.	1	IN	AAAA	2606:50c0:8000::153
improvy.app.	1	IN	AAAA	2606:50c0:8001::153
improvy.app.	1	IN	AAAA	2606:50c0:8002::153
improvy.app.	1	IN	AAAA	2606:50c0:8003::153

;; www → the Pages host. GitHub redirects it to the apex.
www.improvy.app.	1	IN	CNAME	lorenzballe.github.io.
